  "result": "I fixed shell completion for arguments containing `#`.\n\n`split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py` uses `shlex`, which treats `#` as the start of a comment by default. That meant `prog a#b --x` lost everything from the `#` onward, including the word being completed. I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` so `#` is kept as an ordinary character.\n\nI ran `split_arg_string('prog a#b --x=#c')` and it now returns `['prog', 'a#b', '--x=#c']`. The 58 tests in `tests/test_shell_completion.py` pass. I did not rerun the full suite for this change.\n\nI haven't added a regression test for the `#` case, I haven't tried it in a real shell, and nothing is committed.",
